<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Expedition of the Thousand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1860">1860</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Spedizione dei Mille</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Expedition of the Thousand was the campaign led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a> in 1860, in which about a thousand volunteers in red shirts sailed from near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> and landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marsala">Marsala</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in May. They defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> forces, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> and crossed to the mainland, entering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> in September. The fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies</a> opened the way for the proclamation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> in 1861.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/expedition-of-the-thousand.jpg" alt="Expedition of the Thousand" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Partenza_da_Quarto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>That May Giuseppe Garibaldi’s <b>Expedition of the Thousand</b> landed in Sicily and overthrew the Bourbons in the south, and Sardinian troops marched through the Papal Marche and Umbria to meet him.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The new state lasted until Garibaldi's <b>Expedition of the Thousand</b> in 1860 and its annexation to the Kingdom of Italy in 1861.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-naples">Kingdom of Naples · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Cavour’s diplomacy, from the Crimean War to the agreement with Napoleon III at Plombières in 1858, drew France into war with Austria and allowed the kingdom to absorb Lombardy, the central Italian duchies and, after Giuseppe Garibaldi’s <b>Expedition of the Thousand</b>, the south.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>When Giuseppe Garibaldi landed in Sicily in 1860 at the head of the <b>Expedition of the Thousand</b>, with the connivance of Cavour, many rallied to him; he crossed to the mainland and won the Battle of the Volturno with half his army local volunteers, and the Bourbon army…</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The title once carried honour: Giuseppe Garibaldi officially styled himself “Dictator” of Sicily during the <b>Expedition of the Thousand</b> in 1860, and leaders of Poland’s November Uprising of 1830 and January Uprising of 1863 held the same title.</blockquote><a href="/government/dictatorship">Dictatorship · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>Garibaldi's volunteers sang it in the <b>Expedition of the Thousand</b> in 1860, and Giuseppe Verdi chose it to stand for Italy in his &quot;Hymn of the Nations&quot; for the London International Exhibition of 1862.</blockquote><a href="/songs/canto-degli-italiani">Il Canto degli italiani</a></li></ul></section>
